// The Western Interconnection: the western United States, British Columbia,
// Alberta, the El Paso area and Baja California, the northern Mexican state
// synchronised with the Western grid. Baja California Sur (south of 28 N)
// is an isolated system and lies outside the bounds; Sonora is on Mexico's
// national grid and is left out.
//
// Geography is at diorama fidelity: polygons follow the real coastlines and
// interconnection seams closely enough to read on a 60 x 80 grid (about 0.4
// degrees per cell), and a few shores are smoothed where an inlet is
// narrower than a cell. Points are (lon, lat) in degrees.
//
// Seam with the Eastern Interconnection (shared with
// eastern_interconnection.ron): the Alberta-Saskatchewan line (110 W) to the
// 49th parallel, the Montana-Dakota line (104.05 W) to the Nebraska-Colorado
// line, the Colorado border, then south through eastern New Mexico along
// 104.5 W to the Rio Grande.
